{"id":"434d3c43afd7cf17","group":"58","path":"58/batch14/58-df-isomorphism-inhomology.md","title":"Isomorphism in Homology","display":"df-isomorphism-inhomology — Isomorphism in Homology","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-isomorphism-inhomology","aliases":["58-df-isomorphism-inhomology"],"display":"df-isomorphism-inhomology — Isomorphism in Homology","depends_on":["[[../batch15/58-df-chain-complex.md]]","[[../batch09/58-df-zfc-algebra2-chain-map.md]]","[[../batch18/58-df-bijective.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-isomorphism-inhomology"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-isomorphism-inhomology</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-isomorphism-inhomology — Isomorphism in Homology"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"c3537edf2017d84e\" href=\"?note=c3537edf2017d84e\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-chain-complex.md\">../batch15/58-df-chain-complex.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"76a17cf51da75e1a\" href=\"?note=76a17cf51da75e1a\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-zfc-algebra2-chain-map.md\">../batch09/58-df-zfc-algebra2-chain-map.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"d583890235faf0d5\" href=\"?note=d583890235faf0d5\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-bijective.md\">../batch18/58-df-bijective.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\\in V\">\\(f\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"C,D,d_C,d_D\\in V^{\\mathbb Z}\">\\(C,D,d_C,d_D\\in V^{\\mathbb Z}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ChainComplex}_S(C,+_C,d_C)\">\\(\\mathrm{ChainComplex}_S(C,+_C,d_C)\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CycleGroup}_S(n;C,+_C,d_C)\">\\(\\mathrm{CycleGroup}_S(n;C,+_C,d_C)\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BoundaryGroup}_S(n;C,d_C)\">\\(\\mathrm{BoundaryGroup}_S(n;C,d_C)\\)</span> are from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"c3537edf2017d84e\" href=\"?note=c3537edf2017d84e\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-chain-complex.md\">../batch15/58-df-chain-complex.md</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcAlgebra2ChainMap}_S\\subseteq V^7\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcAlgebra2ChainMap}_S\\subseteq V^7\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"76a17cf51da75e1a\" href=\"?note=76a17cf51da75e1a\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-zfc-algebra2-chain-map.md\">../batch09/58-df-zfc-algebra2-chain-map.md</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Bijective}\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{Bijective}\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"d583890235faf0d5\" href=\"?note=d583890235faf0d5\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-bijective.md\">../batch18/58-df-bijective.md</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf H_n(C,+_C,d_C)\">\\(\\mathsf H_n(C,+_C,d_C)\\)</span> is the homology quotient defined here.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{InducedHomologyMap}_S\\subseteq V^9\">\\(\\mathrm{InducedHomologyMap}_S\\subseteq V^9\\)</span> is the induced-map relation defined here.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HomologyIso}_S\\subseteq V^5\">\\(\\mathrm{HomologyIso}_S\\subseteq V^5\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}isomorphism\\text{-}inhomology\\text{-}object}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ChainComplex}_S(C,+_C,d_C)\\land n\\in\\mathbb Z\\to\n\\mathsf H_n(C,+_C,d_C)\\coloneqq\n\\mathrm{CycleGroup}_S(n;C,+_C,d_C)/\\mathrm{BoundaryGroup}_S(n;C,d_C)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}isomorphism\\text{-}inhomology\\text{-}object}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ChainComplex}_S(C,+_C,d_C)\\land n\\in\\mathbb Z\\to\n\\mathsf H_n(C,+_C,d_C)\\coloneqq\n\\mathrm{CycleGroup}_S(n;C,+_C,d_C)/\\mathrm{BoundaryGroup}_S(n;C,d_C)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}isomorphism\\text{-}inhomology\\text{-}map}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{InducedHomologyMap}_S(h,f,n,C,+_C,d_C,D,+_D,d_D)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{ZfcAlgebra2ChainMap}_S(f,C,+_C,d_C,D,+_D,d_D)\\land n\\in\\mathbb Z\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{Function}\\bigl(h,\\mathsf H_n(C,+_C,d_C),\\mathsf H_n(D,+_D,d_D)\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall x\\in\\mathrm{CycleGroup}_S(n;C,+_C,d_C)\\;\nh\\bigl([x]_{\\mathrm{BoundaryGroup}_S(n;C,d_C)}\\bigr)\n=\\bigl[f(n)(x)\\bigr]_{\\mathrm{BoundaryGroup}_S(n;D,d_D)}.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}isomorphism\\text{-}inhomology\\text{-}map}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{InducedHomologyMap}_S(h,f,n,C,+_C,d_C,D,+_D,d_D)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{ZfcAlgebra2ChainMap}_S(f,C,+_C,d_C,D,+_D,d_D)\\land n\\in\\mathbb Z\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{Function}\\bigl(h,\\mathsf H_n(C,+_C,d_C),\\mathsf H_n(D,+_D,d_D)\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall x\\in\\mathrm{CycleGroup}_S(n;C,+_C,d_C)\\;\nh\\bigl([x]_{\\mathrm{BoundaryGroup}_S(n;C,d_C)}\\bigr)\n=\\bigl[f(n)(x)\\bigr]_{\\mathrm{BoundaryGroup}_S(n;D,d_D)}.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}isomorphism\\text{-}inhomology}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{HomologyIso}_S(f,C,D,d_C,d_D)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\exists +_C,+_D\\in V^{\\mathbb Z}\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{ZfcAlgebra2ChainMap}_S(f,C,+_C,d_C,D,+_D,d_D)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall n\\in\\mathbb Z\\;\\exists h\\in V\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{InducedHomologyMap}_S(h,f,n,C,+_C,d_C,D,+_D,d_D)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{Bijective}\\bigl(h,\\mathsf H_n(C,+_C,d_C),\\mathsf H_n(D,+_D,d_D)\\bigr)\\bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}isomorphism\\text{-}inhomology}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{HomologyIso}_S(f,C,D,d_C,d_D)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\exists +_C,+_D\\in V^{\\mathbb Z}\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{ZfcAlgebra2ChainMap}_S(f,C,+_C,d_C,D,+_D,d_D)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall n\\in\\mathbb Z\\;\\exists h\\in V\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{InducedHomologyMap}_S(h,f,n,C,+_C,d_C,D,+_D,d_D)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{Bijective}\\bigl(h,\\mathsf H_n(C,+_C,d_C),\\mathsf H_n(D,+_D,d_D)\\bigr)\\bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The filename follows the existing reference spelling.</li>\n<li>The five-place compatibility predicate keeps the chain-group operations existentially explicit instead of calling the seven-place chain-map predicate with a truncated signature.</li>\n<li>The induced map is defined on quotient classes; the earlier notation <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H_n(f)\">\\(H_n(f)\\)</span> had no defining source.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch15/58-df-chain-complex.md","status":"resolved","id":"c3537edf2017d84e","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-chain-complex.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/58-df-zfc-algebra2-chain-map.md","status":"resolved","id":"76a17cf51da75e1a","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-zfc-algebra2-chain-map.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch18/58-df-bijective.md","status":"resolved","id":"d583890235faf0d5","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-df-bijective.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch15/58-df-chain-complex.md","status":"resolved","id":"c3537edf2017d84e","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{ChainComplex}_S(C,+_C,d_C)$, $\\mathrm{CycleGroup}_S(n;C,+_C,d_C)$, and $\\mathrm{BoundaryGroup}_S(n;C,d_C)$ are from [[../batch15/58-df-chain-complex.md]].","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/58-df-zfc-algebra2-chain-map.md","status":"resolved","id":"76a17cf51da75e1a","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{ZfcAlgebra2ChainMap}_S\\subseteq V^7$ (see [[../batch09/58-df-zfc-algebra2-chain-map.md]]).","embed":false},{"target":"../batch18/58-df-bijective.md","status":"resolved","id":"d583890235faf0d5","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Bijective}\\sub